   "durationS": 16,
   "text": "The Moffat Tunnel cuts through the Continental Divide in north-central Colorado, making a path for both trains and water. This finally provided Denver with a western link through the Continental Divide, something both Cheyenne, Wyoming, and Pueblo already had.",
   "language": "en"
  },
  "2cd470c30cae3315": {
   "url": "/audio/demo/19ffa4674fa7c8e8.mp3",
   "voiceId": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
   "durationS": 23,
   "text": "A station first opened here in 1881, but it burned down. The current structure was erected in two stages, with an enlarged central portion completed in 1914. In 2012, the station underwent a major renovation, transforming it into the centerpiece of a new transit-oriented mixed-use development built on the site's former railyards.",
   "language": "en"
  },
